---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import AudienceCards from "../../components/AudienceCards.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Who It's For"
  description="Start here: a guide to Foundation Framework for teens, parents, church leaders, mentors, and skilled church members."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">Start here</span>
    <h1>One program. Your part in it.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Teens do the learning. Parents, mentors, and church members help them
      grow. The local church brings the people and process together.
    </p>
    <p>
      Foundation Framework connects biblical discipleship with practical skills,
      responsibility, and service. Its purpose is faithfulness in ordinary life,
      built on Jesus Christ. Choose the guide that fits your role; you may have
      more than one.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Find your perspective.</h2>
    <AudienceCards />
  </section>
  <section class="two-column">
    <div>
      <h2>The same learning process.</h2>
      <p>
        A teen chooses a challenge, learns with appropriate help, practices, and
        demonstrates what they have learned. A church-designated adult gives
        feedback and confirms completion. The skill then becomes something to
        use in serving others.
      </p>
      <a href={`${base}how-it-works/`}>See how the program works</a>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>How to use the site today.</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone can read the challenges, adult guides, and printables. My
        Workshop is the participant’s practice tracker; it saves only in the
        current browser. There are no role-based accounts or adult approval
        screens yet. Churches keep their own completion records.
      </p>
      <p>
        The curriculum is sample content for church review. Foundation 7 offers
        an optional starting path, never a prerequisite.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
